      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-07-20T02:45:52Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The peer LMP version isn\u0027t the same as the version of the specification implemented by the peer host.\n\nFor example you can implement 5.2 feature on the host on top of a 5.0 controller (The LMP version would be 5.2 in this case).\n\nSo I don\u0027t think that we want to do this check and only limit EATT for peripherals with a LMP version \u003e\u003d 5.2 as EATT is a host feature, not a controller feature.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 11,
        "startChar": 42,
        "endLine": 11,
        "endChar": 60
      },
      "revId": "2c2659e2c800b2d120dec471b2de203223f6ace4",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "20f563d5_daaa5b03",
        "filename": "/COMMIT_MSG",
        "patchSetId": 6
      },
      "lineNbr": 11,
      "author": {
        "id": 1881539
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-07-20T02:49:39Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e For example you can implement 5.2 feature on the host on top of a 5.0 controller (The LMP version would be 5.2 in this case).\n\n(The LMP version would be 5.0 in this case)*",
      "parentUuid": "0c69a291_e844054b",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 11,
        "startChar": 42,
        "endLine": 11,
        "endChar": 60
      },
      "revId": "2c2659e2c800b2d120dec471b2de203223f6ace4",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "6a2664ee_3beb4b4c",
        "filename": "/COMMIT_MSG",
        "patchSetId": 6
      },
      "lineNbr": 11,
      "author": {
        "id": 1127992
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-07-20T19:01:24Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "LMP or LL version tells what version of Bluetooth LMP or LL specification is supported. \n\nWhile it would be better to check feature bit support, some legacy devices do not respond well to supported EATT feature requests or respond as expected (with error response) when EATT connected. This is a common way to do an IOP fix in these scenarios, and seems to be the best path we have for at least one of the misbehaving devices that bug was filed for.",
      "parentUuid": "20f563d5_daaa5b03",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 11,
        "startChar": 42,
        "endLine": 11,
        "endChar": 60
      },
      "revId": "2c2659e2c800b2d120dec471b2de203223f6ace4",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "206cc247_6e158523",
        "filename": "/COMMIT_MSG",
        "patchSetId": 6
      },
      "lineNbr": 11,
      "author": {
        "id": 1881539
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-07-20T19:32:42Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "What makes you say that it\u0027s a common way to do an IOP fix in these scenarios ?\n\nBecause this change, also prevent devices implementing EATT to use EATT if they happen to have a controller older than 5.2.",
      "parentUuid": "6a2664ee_3beb4b4c",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 11,
        "startChar": 42,
        "endLine": 11,
        "endChar": 60
      },
      "revId": "2c2659e2c800b2d120dec471b2de203223f6ace4",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "6c5389aa_f3ff399c",
        "filename": "/COMMIT_MSG",
        "patchSetId": 6
      },
      "lineNbr": 11,
      "author": {
        "id": 1127992
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-07-20T23:09:32Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Here\u0027s a couple examples of similar logic:\n\nhttps://source.corp.google.com/h/googleplex-android/platform/superproject/main/+/main:packages/modules/Bluetooth/system/stack/smp/smp_act.cc;l\u003d185?q\u003dBTM_ReadRemoteVersion\u0026sq\u003drepo:googleplex-android%2Fplatform%2Fsuperproject%2Fmain%20b:main\n\nhttps://source.corp.google.com/h/googleplex-android/platform/superproject/main/+/main:packages/modules/Bluetooth/system/bta/gatt/bta_gattc_cache.cc;l\u003d178?q\u003dBTM_ReadRemoteVersion\u0026sq\u003drepo:googleplex-android%2Fplatform%2Fsuperproject%2Fmain%20b:main\u0026start\u003d11\n\nAre you aware of any devices that this would impact?\n\nI can change the logic to connect EATT if version not known (this was how it was initially), but can\u0027t think of any other way to solve this. PLMK if you have other ideas.",
      "parentUuid": "206cc247_6e158523",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 11,
        "startChar": 42,
        "endLine": 11,
        "endChar": 60
      },
      "revId": "2c2659e2c800b2d120dec471b2de203223f6ace4",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "ff8a177d_5824ee55",
        "filename": "/COMMIT_MSG",
        "patchSetId": 6
      },
      "lineNbr": 11,
      "author": {
        "id": 1881539
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-07-24T16:43:49Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e Are you aware of any devices that this would impact?\n\nNot explicitly 😞\n\nWe are adding a workaround for an IOP issue, for that we are introducing a behavior that we want to use only for a subset of all Bluetooth devices.\n\nWe cannot target precisely this subset (As we would need to explicitly target a specific Host stack implementation version and we don\u0027t have this information).\nSo instead we are trying to find a superset that encapsulate the population where the issue was found.\n\nWe don\u0027t want this superset to be too big as this means enabling this workaround for devices that don\u0027t have the issue, potentially forcing those devices to create an IOP for us, which would be very bad as it means that those correctly working devices will depend on our IOP workaround.\n\nMy issue here is that our superset is too big as `5.1` is a version that is scheduled for deprecation in 2029 and so designs can still be certified with a 5.1 Controller and might want to use EATT.\n\nI think we should reduce our superset here, a non exhaustive list of what we can use to target devices:\n- Try to read their DID records.\n- Associate this condition with a manufacturer ID.\n- Reduce the version that we target.\n- Any other identifier that we could find.\n\nHowever this mostly requires having the device in hand to look at those, and this might not be the case here. Looking at the bug it seems that the target device controller implements Bluetooth 4.2. So one step here could be to use this instead, even if IMO this is still too big, but is better.\n\nBTW reading the bug, I feel that this IOP should be done inside GATT when we try to read the `SERVER SUPPORTED FEATURES`. As any code that will try to read this attribute is likely to trigger this IOP.\n\nAlso on a side note, I think we should use the IOP database to implement this change as it would make it clearer that this is an IOP. And also it would be good if we document into the code for which devices we encountered this IOP.\n\n\u003e Here\u0027s a couple examples of similar logic:\n\nInteresting, thanks for sharing.\n\nThe GATT robust caching seems not great, but IMO less risky than here, as robust caching is mostly an optimisation and we are just disabling it and I don\u0027t see how the peer could do an IOP with us to circumvent that.\n\nAnd the SMP one is targeting a withdrawn specification version 4.1 to use a weaker security procedure, looking at the associated bug it\u0027s not perfect either but at least the population cannot grow here.\n\n(The path just under that look for 4.2, just disable a different link key derivation function, so it has very little impact.)",
      "parentUuid": "6c5389aa_f3ff399c",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 11,
        "startChar": 42,
        "endLine": 11,
        "endChar": 60
      },
      "revId": "2c2659e2c800b2d120dec471b2de203223f6ace4",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "1b107162_f9fffaeb",
        "filename": "/COMMIT_MSG",
        "patchSetId": 6
      },
      "lineNbr": 11,
      "author": {
        "id": 1127992
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-08-04T20:38:22Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Unfortunately there\u0027s a few known devices exhibiting this problem and specific to certain legacy controllers, but we don\u0027t know full set so relying on manufacturer ID, etc. may be infeasible to address in near term. The set of legacy devices we still support is still much larger than bt 5 devices in the field AFAIK\n\nIIRC server supported features was introduced in 5.2 and some controllers don\u0027t respond to that correctly either, see b/281937405. \n\nThus I think the only option here would be to restrict to LL version \u003c 5.0, WDYT?\n\nalso, EATT is currently only exposed to/used by LE Audio, so I don\u0027t think the impact here is large either ATM given not yet enabled. We will need to revisit it in general before opening up support more broadly",
      "parentUuid": "ff8a177d_5824ee55",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 11,
        "startChar": 42,
        "endLine": 11,
        "endChar": 60
      },
      "revId": "2c2659e2c800b2d120dec471b2de203223f6ace4",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "a1a51153_39a6c389",
        "filename": "/COMMIT_MSG",
        "patchSetId": 6
      },
      "lineNbr": 11,
      "author": {
        "id": 1881539
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-08-04T21:01:33Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e IIRC server supported features was introduced in 5.2 and some controllers don\u0027t respond to that correctly either, see b/281937405.\n\nServer Supported Features is handled in the Host not the Controller.\n\n---\n\n\u003e Thus I think the only option here would be to restrict to LL version \u003c 5.0, WDYT?\n\nYep, I saw that bug, `\u003c 5.0` is `4.2`\n\n\u003e  Looking at the bug it seems that the target device controller implements Bluetooth 4.2. So one step here could be to use this instead, even if IMO this is still too big, but is better.\n\n----\n\n\n\u003e also, EATT is currently only exposed to/used by LE Audio, so I don\u0027t think the impact here is large either ATM given not yet enabled. We will need to revisit it in general before opening up support more broadly\n\nIs it not exposed to the peer as well ? And are we not able to use EATT to access any GATT service exposed by Android ?\n\n\u003e not yet enabled\n\nEATT or LE Audio ?",
      "parentUuid": "1b107162_f9fffaeb",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 11,
        "startChar": 42,
        "endLine": 11,
        "endChar": 60
      },
      "revId": "2c2659e2c800b2d120dec471b2de203223f6ace4",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
